  "summary_text": "Kyle,\n\nPort Washington is running hot and ahead of plan. Yesterday's $479 per groomer matched your trailing 30-day baseline despite a 2% core groom revenue dip week-over-week\u2014that's disciplined execution. More importantly, add-on attach rate jumped to 67% (from 61%), and retail revenue spiked 20%, signaling strong front-of-house momentum and upsell discipline. Month-to-date the store is 5.5% behind DOW-adjusted expectation in absolute dollars, but that's a real performance gap worth watching into November; however, year-to-date you're up 37% in revenue and 35% in appointments, so the underlying business health is undeniable. You should be proud of that trajectory.\n\nHicksville posted a concerning 12% revenue drop yesterday with retail down 66% and transactions down 35%\u2014that's structural weakness, not noise. However, month-to-date Hicksville is actually outperforming: +18% vs prior September and +9.1% vs DOW-adjusted expectation. Yesterday was an outlier; the lapse pool of 193 customers worth $139k annually suggests real opportunity for reactivation. Groomer productivity ($416 MTD) is now tracking above prior month ($379), so the team is improving despite the volatile day.\n\nGlen Cove is severely understaffed. Zero groomers scheduled for today and tomorrow is operationally broken\u2014yesterday's $185 per groomer is 24% below baseline, and you're running on two people. This location needs immediate capacity planning or it becomes a liability. The silver lining: retail attachment is strong (52% up yesterday), but you can't build on that with no production capacity.\n\n**Capacity & coverage:** Port Washington has 7 groomers + 15.0h bathers today and 6 groomers + 15.0h tomorrow; Hicksville has 5 groomers today/tomorrow with 0h bathers; Glen Cove has 0 groomers scheduled today and tomorrow with 0h bathers\u2014next 7 days across all locations: 58 groomer-days with 83.0h bathers (Glen Cove dark for the full week)."
